(a) additional operating cost caused by the redispatching, such as additional fuel costs in the case of upward redispatching, or backup heat provision in the case of downward redispatching of power-generating facilities using high-efficiency cogeneration;

(b) net revenues from the sale of electricity on the day-ahead market that the power-generating, energy storage or demand response facility would have generated without the redispatching request; where financial support is granted to power-generating, energy storage or demand response facilities based on the electricity volume generated or consumed, financial support that would have been received without the redispatching request shall be deemed to be part of the net revenues."},{"id":"reg_2019_943_art37","act":"Regulation (EU) 2019/943 (electricity market regulation)","article":"37","heading":"Tasks of regional coordination centres","url":"https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02019R0943-20240716","version":"consolidated version of 2024-07-16","text":"# Regulation (EU) 2019/943 (electricity market regulation), Article 37: Tasks of regional coordination centres

